  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.35\\ \\text{kg}\"></span> particle is oscillating in simple harmonic motion with an angular frequency of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"7.00\\ \\text{rad s}^{-1}\"></span> and amplitude <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.090\\ \\text{m}\"></span>. At <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 0\"></span>, the displacement is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x(0) = 0.045\\ \\text{m}\"></span> and the velocity is positive.</p><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> </p>Determine the phase constant <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\phi\"></span> in radians.<p>[2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> </p>Write the complete equation for displacement <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x(t)\"></span>.<p>[1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong> </p>Calculate the velocity at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 0\"></span> using the phase angle.<p>[2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"d\"><p><strong>d</strong> </p>Determine the kinetic and potential energies at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 0\"></span>.<p>[2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"e\"><p><strong>e</strong> </p>Explain the significance of phase angle in comparing two SHM systems with identical frequency and amplitude.<p>[1]</p></section>"
